The raw residual block confirms why a naive direct minor check fails: every residual has coefficient `-1` on both lift columns before reduction. The claimed unit minor is therefore a statement about the reduced compatibility matrix, not the unreduced rows. I’m now computing that reduction independently through Singular from the parsed raw ideal, while retaining my own structural checks and controls.
